    {
      "id": "bfddf898b8cf",
      "name": "\u66f4\u65b0 turborepo packages",
      "prompt": "\u57f7\u884c npm package \u66f4\u65b0\u6d41\u7a0b\u81f3 ~/projects/turborepo-starter-kit/\uff1a\n\n1. cd ~/projects/turborepo-starter-kit\n2. \u6aa2\u67e5\u4e26\u5efa\u7acb\u5fc5\u8981\u7684\u74b0\u5883\u8b8a\u6578\uff08apps/api/.env, apps/web/.env\uff09\uff0c\u5f9e env.example \u5efa\u7acb\u4e26\u78ba\u8a8d JWT_SECRET \u662f\u6709\u6548\u503c\n3. \u66f4\u65b0\u6839\u76ee\u9304 dependencies \u5230 latest\uff1a\n   pnpm update --latest\n4. \u66f4\u65b0 apps/api\u3001apps/web\u3001packages/ui \u4e09\u500b workspace \u5230 latest\uff1a\n   pnpm --filter turborepo-starter-kit-api --filter turborepo-starter-kit-web --filter @repo/ui update --latest\n5. \u66f4\u65b0 mobile app\uff1a\n   pnpm mobile:expo:upgrade\n6. \u4fee\u6b63 @types/node \u7248\u672c\uff1apython3 -c \"with open('pnpm-workspace.yaml', 'r') as f: content = f.read(); content = content.replace('\\\"@types/node\\\": ^25.6.0', '\\\"@types/node\\\": \\\"24.12.2\\\"'); open('pnpm-workspace.yaml', 'w').write(content)\"\n7. pnpm install\n8. \u57f7\u884c\u9a57\u8b49\u6d41\u7a0b\uff1apnpm turbo run lint && pnpm turbo run test && pnpm turbo run build\n9. git status \u2014 \u5982\u679c\u6709\u8b8a\u66f4\u624d commit+PR\uff1b\u5982\u679c\u7121\u8b8a\u66f4\uff0c\u901a\u77e5\u4f7f\u7528\u8005\u300c\u2705 turborepo-starter-kit \u6aa2\u67e5\u5b8c\u7562\uff0c\u7121\u65b0 package \u66f4\u65b0\u300d\n10. git checkout -b feat/john/update-packages-$(date +%Y%m%d)\n11. git add package.json pnpm-lock.yaml pnpm-workspace.yaml\n12. git commit -m \"chore(deps): update all packages to latest versions\"\n13. git push -u origin HEAD\n14. gh pr create --title \"chore(deps): update all packages to latest versions\" --body \"## Summary\\nUpdates npm packages to latest in root, apps/api, apps/web, apps/mobile, packages/ui.\\n\\n## Testing\\n- pnpm turbo run lint - passed\\n- pnpm turbo run test - passed\\n- pnpm turbo run build - successful\"",
